---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { collections } from '../data/collections';
import { link } from '../lib/link';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" path="/about" description="About Pinned: a small, fictional Manila enamel-pin label, and the idea underneath it.">
  <header class="container--narrow about-hero">
    <h1 class="about-title font-serif">Small things worth keeping.</h1>
    <p class="about-line">
      Pinned is an independent enamel-pin label based in {site.location}. We make small collectible
      objects about places, things, and the strange reasons we keep them.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="container--narrow section--tight about-prose">
    <p>
      The whole thing started as an argument about souvenirs: why anyone keeps a transit card from a
      city they no longer live in, still holding a small unspendable balance. We didn't resolve the
      argument. We made pins about it instead.
    </p>

    <h2>The name</h2>
    <p>
      A <em>pin</em> holds things in place. <em>Pinning</em> is how you keep something: attach it,
      save it, put it on the board. <em>Pining</em> is the same instinct pointed at something already
      gone. The name sits in the gap between the three. You don't have to notice that to like a pin.
    </p>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <p>
      Designs come out in small batches. Core pins sometimes come back; anything marked
      <em>Limited</em> is a numbered run we don't reprint. Hard enamel, mostly 28–40mm, gold or silver
      plating, rubber clutches as standard.
    </p>

    <h2>The collections</h2>
    <ul class="about-colls">
      {collections.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <a href={link(`/collections/${c.slug}`)}>
            <span class="ac-dot" style={`background:${c.accent}`}></span>
            <strong>{c.name}.</strong> {c.blurb}
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="about-note">
      <h2>One note</h2>
      <p>{site.disclosure}</p>
      <p>
        Adding to cart, saving pins, and checkout all work. They just live in your browser. Treat it
        as a shop that happens not to sell anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section--tight">
    <Newsletter source="about" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding-block: var(--sp-7) var(--sp-4);
  }
  .about-title {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .about-line {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
    max-width: 54ch;
  }
  .about-prose { font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.75; }
  .about-prose p { margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .about-prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: var(--sp-5) 0 var(--sp-2);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .about-prose em { color: var(--ink); font-style: italic; }
  .about-colls {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .about-colls li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    padding: var(--sp-3) 0;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .about-colls li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .about-colls a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .about-colls a:hover strong { color: var(--brand-ink); }
  .about-colls strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .ac-dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .about-note {
    margin-top: var(--sp-5);
    padding-top: var(--sp-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .about-note h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .about-note p { font-size: var(--step-0); }
</style>
